## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests lifecycle management, reproducibility, and safe feature releases in a privacy-conscious SageMaker setup.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Experiments and Model Registry
- Canary deployments and rollback strategies
- Drift and quality monitoring with lightweight checks
- PrivateLink isolation and VPC security

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: create an Experiment and a Trial
import { SageMakerClient, CreateExperimentCommand, CreateTrialCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker";
const c = new SageMakerClient({region: 'us-east-1'});
async function init() {
  const exp = await c.send(new CreateExperimentCommand({ExperimentName: 'TextClassifier_V1'}));
  await c.send(new CreateTrialCommand({TrialName: 'V1_Run', ExperimentName: exp.ExperimentArn}));
}
```

